 "notes": [
  "On 4h, OBV crossing up through its SMA 20 gave 2,803 entries in 748 separate moves. Twenty candles later they were 0.14% ahead of random entries, inside the luck band of -0.26 to 0.22. Holding while OBV stayed above the SMA 20 landed at 0.17%, also inside the band. On 1h the same cross gave 11,104 entries and also did the same as random.",
  "The short side changes with the trend. On 1h, when the pair closed below its 200-day SMA, a cross down through the SMA 20 gave 4,681 entries in 1,352 moves. Price fell 0.15% more than after random downtrend candles, above a band of -0.09 to 0.08. It held without its strongest stretch, signals on May 10–12, 2022 during the Terra collapse, and at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles. In uptrends the same cross was the same as random, at -0.04%.",
  "On daily, holding long while OBV was above its SMA 20 beat random by 2.87%. That gap comes from 308 entries between Sep 2, 2020 and Dec 28, 2021, and without them it is chance. In uptrends it beat random by 3.66%, again resting on one stretch. In downtrends it was the same as random at -0.78%, and no single pair had enough separate moves to be judged on its own.",
  "Daily crosses up through the moving average tended to come late. OBV crossing up its EMA 50 did 3.16% worse than random, and on ETH 6.81% worse, a result that held without its strongest stretch and at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles. On BTC, a cross up through the SMA 20 did 2.97% worse than random and held without its strongest stretch, but not at 50 or 100 candles. In downtrends the EMA 50 cross was the same as random.",
  "Some results rest on one stretch. On 4h, ETH's cross up through the SMA 20 beat random only because of signals between Dec 31, 2020 and Jan 2, 2021. On daily, BTC's short on a cross down through the SMA 20 beat random by 2.54% on the strength of 3 entries between Jun 1, 2022 and Jun 7, 2022. Treat both as stretch effects.",
  "For a long DCA bot on these pairs, an OBV cross over its SMA 20 or EMA 50 adds no timing, so the DCA orders and take profit do the work. The one shape worth testing is a filter for short bots on 1h: a cross down through the SMA 20 only while price is below its 200-day SMA. On daily, consider leaving the EMA 50 cross up out of a long bot's start conditions."
 ],
